WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.835
Today we go behind that power grab.

00:00:01.835 --> 00:00:03.236
That was that wasn't.

00:00:03.236 --> 00:00:05.005
Or what was it exactly, Will?

00:00:05.005 --> 00:00:05.438
Right now,

00:00:05.438 --> 00:00:06.940
we're going to try to answer

00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:08.942
all of the questions that we have

00:00:08.942 --> 00:00:10.844
about the revolt inside Russia.

00:00:10.844 --> 00:00:12.445
The mercenary who led

00:00:12.445 --> 00:00:13.113
what looked

00:00:13.113 --> 00:00:14.914
and sounded like a revolt

00:00:14.914 --> 00:00:15.382
is now

00:00:15.382 --> 00:00:17.384
trying to answer one of those questions.

00:00:17.384 --> 00:00:18.251
Why?

00:00:18.251 --> 00:00:19.519
CNN just obtained

00:00:19.519 --> 00:00:20.920
New audio of Prigozhin,

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:22.956
and he says the march to Moscow

00:00:22.956 --> 00:00:25.759
was not a coup, but only a protest.

00:00:26.926 --> 00:00:27.660
You know, somebody

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:28.561
saying you

00:00:28.561 --> 00:00:30.463
two factors played into my decision

00:00:30.463 --> 00:00:31.664
to turn around.

00:00:31.664 --> 00:00:32.465
First factor,

00:00:32.465 --> 00:00:34.734
we wanted to avoid a Russian bloodshed.

00:00:34.734 --> 00:00:35.435
Second is

00:00:35.435 --> 00:00:37.604
we marched in demonstration of a protest

00:00:37.737 --> 00:00:39.873
not to overturn the power in the country

00:00:40.373 --> 00:00:41.241
at this time.

00:00:41.241 --> 00:00:43.510
Alexander Lukashenko extended his hand

00:00:43.643 --> 00:00:45.645
and offered to find solutions

00:00:45.645 --> 00:00:47.814
for the further work of Wagner, PMC

00:00:47.814 --> 00:00:49.049
and legal jurisdiction.

00:00:50.350 --> 00:00:51.418
CNN is covering this

00:00:51.418 --> 00:00:53.820
story from all corners of the globe.

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:55.088
We're going to start our coverage

00:00:55.088 --> 00:00:57.724
in London with CNN's Nic Robertson.

00:00:57.724 --> 00:01:01.461
Nic, a pretty remarkable response

00:01:01.461 --> 00:01:02.162
that we are hearing

00:01:02.162 --> 00:01:03.329
for the first time

00:01:03.329 --> 00:01:05.832
from the mercenary leader,

00:01:06.232 --> 00:01:08.334
but it does also seem to comport

00:01:08.334 --> 00:01:10.437
with the big ongoing argument

00:01:10.437 --> 00:01:12.505
that Prigozhin had been having

00:01:12.505 --> 00:01:15.075
with the defense minister, Sergei Shoigu.

00:01:15.642 --> 00:01:17.310
What we learned from Prigozhin,

00:01:17.310 --> 00:01:18.511
not just that he's saying

00:01:18.511 --> 00:01:20.380
I wasn't trying to overthrow Putin

00:01:20.380 --> 00:01:22.449
and we didn't mean or intend

00:01:22.449 --> 00:01:24.184
to go out and kill any Russian troops.

00:01:24.184 --> 00:01:25.051
They fired on us.

00:01:25.051 --> 00:01:26.586
First walking by the helicopters.

00:01:26.586 --> 00:01:28.822
He now says he shot down

00:01:28.822 --> 00:01:31.691
But he says this was a march for justice.

00:01:31.691 --> 00:01:33.159
His call that it was a march,

00:01:33.159 --> 00:01:35.161
he said, to try to keep his Wagner

00:01:35.161 --> 00:01:38.932
pm say his Wagner mercenary group alive.

00:01:39.332 --> 00:01:40.500
He says in the audio

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:42.635
recording that it was going to be forced

00:01:42.635 --> 00:01:44.704
to shut down on the 1st of July,

00:01:44.704 --> 00:01:45.805
that he had talked

00:01:45.805 --> 00:01:47.140
among the commanding officers

00:01:47.140 --> 00:01:48.374
and with the men

00:01:48.374 --> 00:01:49.309
and barely

00:01:49.309 --> 00:01:51.277
any of them had agreed to

00:01:51.277 --> 00:01:52.812
down tools for Wagner

00:01:52.812 --> 00:01:54.781
and sign up for Russia's military

00:01:54.781 --> 00:01:56.883
as was being demanded of them.

00:01:56.883 --> 00:01:59.519
And he wanted to keep Wagner alive.

00:01:59.819 --> 00:02:00.887
This is what he's saying.

00:02:00.887 --> 00:02:02.222
And he goes on to say

00:02:02.222 --> 00:02:03.990
when he was speaking to Lukashenko

00:02:03.990 --> 00:02:04.591
and the reason

00:02:04.591 --> 00:02:07.026
he accepted the Russian president's

00:02:07.026 --> 00:02:09.596
offer to go and be an exile

00:02:09.596 --> 00:02:11.164
there was because Lukashenko

00:02:11.164 --> 00:02:12.065
offered him a way

00:02:12.065 --> 00:02:15.902
for a legal jurisdiction for PMC Wagner

00:02:16.035 --> 00:02:16.803
to keep

00:02:16.803 --> 00:02:18.671
his private military contracting

00:02:18.671 --> 00:02:20.473
company up and running.

00:02:20.473 --> 00:02:22.675
This has been about power

00:02:22.675 --> 00:02:24.477
and it's been about money.

00:02:24.477 --> 00:02:26.012
Prigozhin has been

00:02:26.012 --> 00:02:27.647
trying to fight off Russia's

00:02:27.647 --> 00:02:28.781
defense minister

00:02:28.781 --> 00:02:30.650
from taking control of Wagner,

00:02:30.650 --> 00:02:31.451
his men

00:02:31.451 --> 00:02:33.219
and the financial income potentially

00:02:33.219 --> 00:02:34.120
that comes from it.

00:02:34.120 --> 00:02:35.288
But I think one of the point

00:02:35.288 --> 00:02:35.822
comes through

00:02:35.822 --> 00:02:36.890
in this recording, and again,

00:02:36.890 --> 00:02:38.224
we don't know when it was made.

00:02:38.224 --> 00:02:40.560
But again, he takes a pot shot

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:41.661
at Sergei

00:02:41.661 --> 00:02:43.029
Shoigu, the defense minister,

00:02:43.029 --> 00:02:44.998
saying that this march was a protest

00:02:44.998 --> 00:02:47.400
about the way the war was being run.

00:02:47.567 --> 00:02:49.702
This is a very destructive message

00:02:49.702 --> 00:02:50.670
for Putin

00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:53.473
to continue to hear made publicly.

00:02:53.973 --> 00:02:54.274
Oh, wow.

00:02:54.274 --> 00:02:56.109
There is so much to unpack there.

00:02:56.109 --> 00:02:56.843
Thank you so much.

00:02:56.843 --> 00:02:59.279
For that critical, critical context.

00:02:59.646 --> 00:03:01.281
Nick, I want to go now to Nick

00:03:01.281 --> 00:03:03.316
Paton Walsh, who is in Kiev,

00:03:03.316 --> 00:03:04.350
Ukraine's capital.

00:03:04.350 --> 00:03:06.853
So, Nick, how will progressions comments

00:03:07.220 --> 00:03:09.289
That this was a protest and not a coup?

00:03:09.289 --> 00:03:10.990
And what he specifically said

00:03:10.990 --> 00:03:12.358
that Nick was just reporting

00:03:12.358 --> 00:03:14.594
about the way that the war inside

00:03:14.594 --> 00:03:16.062
Russia is being prosecuted?

00:03:16.062 --> 00:03:17.263
How will that land

00:03:17.263 --> 00:03:18.331
where you are in Ukraine?

00:03:20.767 --> 00:03:22.669
Yeah, I mean, it's sort of everything

00:03:22.669 --> 00:03:25.038
relevant to some degree to Ukrainians,

00:03:25.038 --> 00:03:26.406
so long as this remarkable

00:03:26.406 --> 00:03:27.507
revenge tragedy

00:03:27.507 --> 00:03:29.576
drama continues to play out.

00:03:29.609 --> 00:03:31.110
Yevgeny Prigozhin showing

00:03:31.110 --> 00:03:33.146
miscalculation, perhaps or not,

00:03:33.146 --> 00:03:35.148
telling us the entirety of the story

00:03:35.148 --> 00:03:36.583
that he somehow thought

00:03:36.583 --> 00:03:38.851
he could take his troops, as he says,

00:03:39.185 --> 00:03:40.853
hundreds of miles on the road

00:03:40.853 --> 00:03:42.055
up to Moscow

00:03:42.055 --> 00:03:44.057
and then suddenly change his mind

00:03:44.057 --> 00:03:45.758
and not have Russian President

00:03:45.758 --> 00:03:46.459
Vladimir Putin

00:03:46.459 --> 00:03:47.827
think that that might have been

00:03:47.827 --> 00:03:50.163
a challenge to the Kremlin, had himself

00:03:50.296 --> 00:03:53.299
so keen to point out this notion of it

00:03:53.299 --> 00:03:55.068
basically being a protest about

00:03:55.068 --> 00:03:57.270
how Wagner was being treated

00:03:57.270 --> 00:03:58.605
and the conduct of the war

00:03:58.605 --> 00:03:59.505
rather than the challenge

00:03:59.505 --> 00:04:00.506
to Moscow itself.

00:04:00.506 --> 00:04:02.008
But this continues, as it seems.

00:04:02.008 --> 00:04:03.476
Does progressions believe

00:04:03.476 --> 00:04:04.978
that he can keep Virginia

00:04:04.978 --> 00:04:05.678
as a group

00:04:05.678 --> 00:04:07.914
alive, possibly inside of Belarus?

00:04:07.914 --> 00:04:09.249
That's somewhat startling.

00:04:09.249 --> 00:04:10.984
It may never indeed happen,

00:04:10.984 --> 00:04:12.051
and we don't exactly know

00:04:12.051 --> 00:04:12.752
where Prigozhin is

00:04:12.752 --> 00:04:14.120
when he recorded this message.

00:04:14.120 --> 00:04:15.955
He doesn't spell that out.

00:04:15.955 --> 00:04:16.623
What does it mean

00:04:16.623 --> 00:04:17.690
for Ukrainian officials?

00:04:17.690 --> 00:04:18.091
Well,

00:04:18.091 --> 00:04:18.925
it certainly means

00:04:18.925 --> 00:04:20.727
that Vadim may continue to exist.

00:04:20.727 --> 00:04:22.262
It certainly means that the question

00:04:22.262 --> 00:04:23.463
of all this functionality

00:04:23.463 --> 00:04:25.331
on the front lines hasn't been resolved,

00:04:25.331 --> 00:04:27.033
and that could mean further tension

00:04:27.033 --> 00:04:28.201
between the fighters

00:04:28.201 --> 00:04:29.569
being asked to step down

00:04:29.569 --> 00:04:30.970
and the regular Russian military

00:04:30.970 --> 00:04:31.604
being asked

00:04:31.604 --> 00:04:33.740
to try and ensure that occurs.

00:04:33.740 --> 00:04:34.574
We've seen since

00:04:34.574 --> 00:04:36.276
this began suggestions

00:04:36.276 --> 00:04:38.645
that Ukraine is continuing to advance

00:04:38.645 --> 00:04:40.380
possibly at the normal pace

00:04:40.380 --> 00:04:42.048
of the past weeks in certain

00:04:42.048 --> 00:04:42.982
key areas near

00:04:42.982 --> 00:04:44.350
the symbolic city of Bachman.

00:04:44.350 --> 00:04:46.419
We have fought so hard over the winter,

00:04:46.653 --> 00:04:47.820
possibly in the south,

00:04:47.820 --> 00:04:48.588
to where they're claiming

00:04:48.588 --> 00:04:48.921
to take

00:04:48.921 --> 00:04:50.256
another village as well,

00:04:50.256 --> 00:04:50.823
and also

00:04:50.823 --> 00:04:52.859
another advance unexpected in the far

00:04:52.925 --> 00:04:55.161
west of the front lines

00:04:55.161 --> 00:04:57.864
near the river near the city of Hesse on.

00:04:58.031 --> 00:04:59.399
So things changing.

00:04:59.399 --> 00:05:00.366
But I think really

00:05:00.366 --> 00:05:01.634
the central message from

00:05:01.634 --> 00:05:02.869
this is Prigozhin

00:05:02.869 --> 00:05:04.470
perhaps stepping down,

00:05:04.470 --> 00:05:05.905
not necessarily offering

00:05:05.905 --> 00:05:06.406
we think

00:05:06.406 --> 00:05:07.173
I think

00:05:07.173 --> 00:05:08.174
a full explanation

00:05:08.174 --> 00:05:09.242
as to his extraordinary

00:05:09.242 --> 00:05:10.910
change of heart on the road,

00:05:10.910 --> 00:05:11.978
definitely tallying

00:05:11.978 --> 00:05:13.112
with the Kremlin's message

00:05:13.112 --> 00:05:14.580
as of yesterday.

00:05:14.580 --> 00:05:16.616
But it is still a startling,

00:05:16.616 --> 00:05:17.150
I think,

00:05:17.150 --> 00:05:19.085
vacuum of power to some degree

00:05:19.085 --> 00:05:19.652
at the heart

00:05:19.652 --> 00:05:21.321
of the Russian government here,

00:05:21.321 --> 00:05:22.522
the defense minister

00:05:22.522 --> 00:05:24.691
releasing prerecorded videos, Vladimir

00:05:24.691 --> 00:05:26.759
Putin releasing prerecorded videos.

00:05:26.759 --> 00:05:28.561
The live respondent has still

00:05:28.561 --> 00:05:29.962
Yevgeny Prigozhin,

00:05:29.962 --> 00:05:30.963
and that may be something

00:05:30.963 --> 00:05:32.765
the Kremlin have to answer

00:05:32.765 --> 00:05:34.200
in the days or hours ahead

00:05:34.200 --> 00:05:36.436
just to reassure their own troops

00:05:36.636 --> 00:05:37.370
that there's somebody

00:05:37.370 --> 00:05:38.871
with their hand on the wheel.

00:05:38.871 --> 00:05:41.407
Putin likes to basically set his own

00:05:41.407 --> 00:05:43.476
agenda and appear when he feels like it.

00:05:43.476 --> 00:05:44.043
But these are very

00:05:44.043 --> 00:05:45.578
different circumstances.

00:05:45.578 --> 00:05:46.412
And yet again,

00:05:46.412 --> 00:05:48.448
we just seem to see a Russian elite here

00:05:48.748 --> 00:05:49.982
miss communicating,

00:05:49.982 --> 00:05:50.850
mis imagining

00:05:50.850 --> 00:05:52.418
exactly what they can get away with.

00:05:52.418 --> 00:05:54.087
Reverse that chart,

00:05:54.087 --> 00:05:56.022
of course, exceptionally quickly.

00:05:56.022 --> 00:05:58.491
Prigozhin Putin pardoning Prigozhin

00:05:58.691 --> 00:06:00.360
startling series of affairs

00:06:00.360 --> 00:06:02.362
and one that I'm sure Ukraine will hope

00:06:02.362 --> 00:06:04.697
will yield disarray on the front lines

00:06:04.697 --> 00:06:06.499
in the days or weeks ahead. Donna.

00:06:06.499 --> 00:06:07.300
No question.

00:06:07.300 --> 00:06:08.167
And we are just

00:06:08.167 --> 00:06:09.469
really trying to read the tea

00:06:09.469 --> 00:06:11.604
leaves on a lot of these statements

00:06:11.604 --> 00:06:13.639
that we're getting in the last hour

00:06:13.639 --> 00:06:15.641
from Prigozhin. From Prigozhin, rather.

00:06:15.641 --> 00:06:16.776
Thank you so much for that.

00:06:16.776 --> 00:06:18.945
I want to go back to the United States

00:06:18.945 --> 00:06:19.979
and over to the Pentagon

00:06:19.979 --> 00:06:21.981
where CNN's Natasha Bertrand is.

00:06:21.981 --> 00:06:24.250
So Natasha Wagner's mercenary leader.

00:06:24.250 --> 00:06:25.651
We were just talking about

00:06:25.651 --> 00:06:27.787
he says this wasn't a coup attempt.

00:06:27.787 --> 00:06:29.389
And specifically

00:06:29.389 --> 00:06:30.857
what he said is that

00:06:30.857 --> 00:06:32.725
this was a quote unquote protest.

00:06:32.725 --> 00:06:34.293
And what he's protesting

00:06:34.293 --> 00:06:36.396
is the idea that the Russian military

00:06:36.662 --> 00:06:39.165
was trying to dissolve this Wagner

00:06:39.165 --> 00:06:41.701
mercenary group and do so by July 1st.

00:06:42.068 --> 00:06:42.802
Do your sources

00:06:42.802 --> 00:06:45.238
there at the Pentagon, in the military

00:06:45.905 --> 00:06:47.006
an American military,

00:06:47.006 --> 00:06:49.242
believe that that's the case?

00:06:49.242 --> 00:06:49.742
Well, Don,

00:06:49.742 --> 00:06:52.011
this actually does comport with U.S.

00:06:52.011 --> 00:06:53.079
officials understanding

00:06:53.079 --> 00:06:54.714
broadly of what was motivating

00:06:54.714 --> 00:06:55.848
Prigozhin in the days

00:06:55.848 --> 00:06:58.117
leading up to this rebellion.

00:06:58.151 --> 00:06:58.885
As you'll recall,

00:06:58.885 --> 00:07:00.686
we did report over the weekend that U.S.

00:07:00.686 --> 00:07:02.054
intelligence did see signs

00:07:02.054 --> 00:07:02.922
that Prigozhin

00:07:02.922 --> 00:07:03.790
was plotting

00:07:03.790 --> 00:07:05.591
a potential major challenge to Russia's

00:07:05.591 --> 00:07:06.592
military leadership.

00:07:06.592 --> 00:07:08.227
And that was because

00:07:08.227 --> 00:07:08.961
of the fact

00:07:08.961 --> 00:07:09.729
that it appeared

00:07:09.729 --> 00:07:10.596
that Russia's military

00:07:10.596 --> 00:07:11.731
leadership was preparing

00:07:11.731 --> 00:07:12.965
to usurp Faulkner

00:07:12.965 --> 00:07:14.634
and try to absorb it

00:07:14.634 --> 00:07:16.636
within the Russian military ranks.

00:07:16.636 --> 00:07:18.171
And so what Prigozhin is saying here

00:07:18.171 --> 00:07:19.172
essentially is that

00:07:19.172 --> 00:07:20.373
he did not want to

00:07:20.373 --> 00:07:21.874
overthrow the Russian government.

00:07:21.874 --> 00:07:24.010
Now, it is unclear to US officials,

00:07:24.310 --> 00:07:25.211
including in the run

00:07:25.211 --> 00:07:26.012
up to this rebellion,

00:07:26.012 --> 00:07:28.281
what his ultimate aim actually was,

00:07:28.281 --> 00:07:30.149
if he wanted to only challenge

00:07:30.149 --> 00:07:31.584
Russia's defense leaders

00:07:31.584 --> 00:07:33.419
and perhaps spark change in that area,

00:07:33.419 --> 00:07:35.254
or if he actually wanted

00:07:35.254 --> 00:07:37.156
to try to overthrow Vladimir Putin.

00:07:37.156 --> 00:07:38.491
As we saw over the weekend,

00:07:38.491 --> 00:07:40.560
he did march towards Moscow.

00:07:40.560 --> 00:07:42.128
And so that raised a lot of questions

00:07:42.128 --> 00:07:42.528
in U.S.

00:07:42.528 --> 00:07:43.262
official minds

00:07:43.262 --> 00:07:45.631
about what he was actually doing.

00:07:45.631 --> 00:07:45.932
U.S.

00:07:45.932 --> 00:07:46.766
intelligence officials

00:07:46.766 --> 00:07:47.700
were surprised, though,

00:07:47.700 --> 00:07:49.702
that this wasn't a bloodier affair.

00:07:49.702 --> 00:07:52.004
They believe that it is

00:07:52.004 --> 00:07:52.872
that it is surprising

00:07:52.872 --> 00:07:53.739
that Russia's troops

00:07:53.739 --> 00:07:55.341
did not fight back harder.

00:07:55.341 --> 00:07:56.776
And that is one of the main questions

00:07:56.776 --> 00:07:57.877
that they're asking now is

00:07:57.877 --> 00:07:58.878
why did

00:07:58.878 --> 00:08:00.680
Russia did Wagner troops face

00:08:00.680 --> 00:08:02.882
so little resistance from Russian troops?

00:08:02.882 --> 00:08:04.383
But just in terms broadly

00:08:04.383 --> 00:08:06.652
of what Prigozhin is saying here, U.S.

00:08:06.652 --> 00:08:08.020
officials are monitoring

00:08:08.020 --> 00:08:08.888
whether he is able

00:08:08.888 --> 00:08:10.156
to reconstitute himself,

00:08:10.156 --> 00:08:11.524
whether he is going to go

00:08:11.524 --> 00:08:13.392
into exile in Belarus

00:08:13.392 --> 00:08:15.328
and just how the Wagner forces

00:08:15.328 --> 00:08:16.929
are actually going to be absorbed

00:08:16.929 --> 00:08:18.164
within the Russian military

00:08:18.164 --> 00:08:20.333
after months and months of Prigozhin

00:08:20.333 --> 00:08:21.267
telling them

00:08:21.267 --> 00:08:22.568
that the Russian Ministry of Defense

00:08:22.568 --> 00:08:23.736
cannot be trusted

00:08:23.736 --> 00:08:24.470
and has essentially

00:08:24.470 --> 00:08:26.472
left them to die in Ukraine. Yeah.

00:08:26.472 --> 00:08:28.341
Or if they will at all, considering

00:08:28.341 --> 00:08:28.708
the fact

00:08:28.708 --> 00:08:29.642
that it looks like

00:08:29.642 --> 00:08:30.910
Prigozhin is suggesting

00:08:30.910 --> 00:08:32.311
in this audio

00:08:32.311 --> 00:08:33.913
recording that was just released

